**ARTICLE XIV - INDEMNIFICATION**

14.1 **Indemnification Obligations**: Each party (the "Indemnifying Party") shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the other parties (the "Indemnified Parties") from and against any and all claims, damages, losses, liabilities, costs, or expenses (including reasonable attorney's fees and court costs) arising out of or resulting from:

- (a) Any negligent act or omission of the Indemnifying Party, its agents, employees, or subcontractors in connection with the performance of this Agreement.
- (b) Any breach of this Agreement by the Indemnifying Party.
- (c) Any violation of applicable laws, regulations, or ordinances by the Indemnifying Party.

14.2 **Notification of Claims**: The Indemnified Parties shall promptly notify the Indemnifying Party in writing of any claim for which indemnification is sought under this Article. Failure to provide timely notice shall not relieve the Indemnifying Party of its indemnification obligations, except to the extent that such delay materially prejudices the Indemnifying Party's ability to defend against the claim.

14.3 **Control of Defense**: The Indemnifying Party shall have the right to control the defense and settlement of any claim for which indemnification is sought, provided that it shall not settle any claim without the Indemnified Parties' prior written consent, which shall not be unreasonably withheld. The Indemnified Parties shall cooperate with the Indemnifying Party in the defense of any such claim.

14.4 **Additional Indemnification for Subcontractors**: In the event that any subcontractors are engaged in the performance of this Agreement, each party shall ensure that such subcontractors agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the parties in a manner consistent with this Article. Each party shall be responsible for any failure of its subcontractors to comply with this indemnification provision.

---

**ARTICLE XV - DISPUTE RESOLUTION**

15.1 **Negotiation**: In the event of any dispute arising out of or relating to this Agreement, the parties agree to first attempt to resolve the dispute through informal negotiations. A party wishing to initiate negotiations shall provide written notice to the other parties, specifying the nature of the dispute. The parties shall meet within ten (10) business days of receipt of such notice to discuss the matter in good faith.

15.2 **Mediation**: If the dispute cannot be resolved through negotiation, the parties agree to submit the dispute to mediation before a mutually agreed-upon mediator. The mediation shall take place within thirty (30) days of the written notice of the failure to negotiate, and the parties shall share the costs of the mediation equally.

15.3 **Arbitration**: If the dispute remains unresolved after mediation, the parties agree to submit the dispute to binding arbitration in accordance with the rules of the American Arbitration Association (AAA). The arbitration shall take place in [Insert Location], and the decision of the arbitrator shall be final and binding on all parties. Each party shall bear its own costs and expenses associated with the arbitration, except that the prevailing party shall be entitled to recover reasonable attorney’s fees and costs from the other party.

15.4 **Confidentiality**: All negotiations and mediation proceedings conducted under this Article shall be confidential and shall not be disclosed to any third party without the prior written consent of all parties involved, except as required by law.

---

**ARTICLE XVI - ASSIGNMENT AND SUBCONTRACTING**

16.1 **Assignment**: No party may assign or transfer its rights or obligations under this Agreement without the prior written consent of the other parties, which shall not be unreasonably withheld. Any attempted assignment without such consent shall be deemed null and void.

16.2 **Subcontracting**: Each party may subcontract portions of its obligations under this Agreement, provided that it shall remain fully responsible for the performance of its obligations and for the acts and omissions of its subcontractors. Each party shall notify the other parties in writing prior to subcontracting any significant portion of its obligations, detailing the qualifications and experience of the proposed subcontractor.

16.3 **Continuity of Services**: In the event that a party subcontracts any portion of its obligations, it shall ensure that the subcontractor adheres to the same standards of quality and service as required under this Agreement. The parties agree that any subcontracting shall not relieve the primary party of its obligations and responsibilities under this Agreement.

---

**ARTICLE XVII - TERMINATION**

17.1 **Termination for Convenience**: Any party may terminate this Agreement for any reason upon providing thirty (30) days’ written notice to the other parties. Termination shall not affect any rights or obligations that have accrued prior to the effective date of termination.

17.2 **Termination for Cause**: A party may terminate this Agreement immediately upon written notice if any other party breaches any material term or condition of this Agreement and fails to cure such breach within fifteen (15) business days after receiving written notice of such breach.

17.3 **Effect of Termination**: Upon termination of this Agreement, all rights and obligations of the parties shall cease, except for those obligations expressly stated to survive termination, including but not limited to indemnification obligations, confidentiality provisions, and any payment obligations for services rendered prior to termination.

